    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusader</a> army left a well-watered position at La Saphorie against the advice of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raymond-iii-of-tripoli">Raymond III of Tripoli</a> and the Hospitallers, and marched in July heat to a dry plateau where it was surrounded.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> ordered the execution of about 200 Templar and Hospitaller knights and of captured Turcopoles, spared the other captive barons, and had <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raynald-of-chatillon">Raynald of Châtillon</a> killed for breaking a truce.</li><li>With the field army gone and the castles thinly held, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusader</a> kingdom fell quickly, and the defeat led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>'s son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-afdal">al-Afdal</a>, then 17, watched the battle beside his father. He later described how Saladin told him they had not beaten the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guy-of-lusignan">Guy</a>'s tent fell, and when it fell Saladin dismounted, prostrated himself and wept for joy.</p></aside>
    </section>

